      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "High glycemic index foods can cause rapid spikes in blood sugar levels, as they are quickly digested and absorbed. Low glycemic index foods, on the other hand, have a slower, steadier release of sugar, leading to less dramatic blood sugar fluctuations. Properly managing these fluctuations is important for insulin, a hormone that helps regulate blood sugar. Consuming mostly low glycemic index foods can assist in avoiding insulin resistance and diabetes, maintaining overall health.",
